This code reads the magnitude of the MPU6050 accelerometer every 200ms for a total of 15 iterations, maintains a rolling window of the last ten magnitude readings, computes the mean and standard deviation of that window while enforcing a minimum standard deviation of 1.0 to avoid division by zero, calculates the z-score for each new sample and logs a warning whenever the absolute z-score exceeds 3.0. It also handles I2C communication errors gracefully and ensures that the I2C bus is cleanly released when the program exits. The MQTT client is used to log the z-score warnings to an MQTT broker.

